editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title The pier names its own zone -- REDS %90 closed by a host hand
prompt Keaton ran nixos/rebuild-outer.sh on the host and pasted the transcript
think Verified before claiming, because the whole point of this red was a declared zone the ground did not carry -- taking a successful rebuild transcript as proof of the property would have repeated the original error one level up. Read the three facts directly instead: date now prints EDT, /etc/localtime resolves into the tzdata store path for America/New_York where it resolved to nothing at all before, and the zone scan answers ZONE_OK.
think Then ran the witness itself rather than only its zone duty, since a red closes on a witness and not on the piece of it that happens to be interesting. All four duties GREEN -- shape, monotonicity, zone by name, provenance -- and the provenance line now reports zone=America/New_York with a 0s delta against the host clock, which is the same duty that has been quietly passing all along only because every caller passed TZ by hand.
obs The division of labour is the honest part of this row. The fix was one line in this pier's own tracked configuration.nix, which an agent can write; the closing was an activation on the host outside the jail, which an agent cannot run. Naming that boundary rather than blurring it is why the row stood open through three rounds instead of being claimed when the line landed.
obs A bare date on this pier is now correct for the first time. The one-clock discipline held throughout by explicit TZ, so no stamp was ever wrong -- what changes is that the ground no longer disagrees with the profile beside it, and the next hand that forgets the flag is no longer punished for it.
loom one_clock duties_green=4 zone=America/New_York provenance_delta_s=0 localtime=resolved
file crux/REDS.md REDS %90 closed with the three facts read directly rather than inferred from the transcript
recommend keep-going every red booked in this session's arc now stands closed except %91's own successor work, which is optional rather than owed -- the room sweep left no page over-claiming, so a later pass may promote pages toward Checkable one at a time, each promotion earning its own witness citation.
